-- title:
--   Unique parabolic extension of a character across -1
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, let $A$ be an additive abelian group, and let $\psi$ be an additive homomorphism from $\Gamma$, regarded as an additive group via `Additive`, to $A$ (equivalently, a homomorphism of groups $\Gamma \to A$). Assume $\psi$ is parabolic in the sense of the predicate [`ModularCurve.Period.IsParabolicHom`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L15): for every $\gamma \in \Gamma$ whose underlying integer matrix satisfies $(\operatorname{tr}\gamma)^2 = 4$, one has $\psi(\gamma) = 0$. Write $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$ for the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma$ together with the integer powers of $-1$. The assertion is that there is exactly one additive homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$ (again viewed additively) to $A$ with the two properties: $\varphi$ is parabolic, i.e. $\varphi(\delta) = 0$ for every $\delta$ in $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$ with $(\operatorname{tr}\delta)^2 = 4$; and $\varphi$ restricts to $\psi$ along the inclusion, i.e. $\varphi(\gamma) = \psi(\gamma)$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma$, where on the left $\gamma$ is viewed as an element of the larger subgroup.
--
--   This says that parabolic characters do not see the centre: restriction along $\Gamma \hookrightarrow \pm\Gamma$ is a bijection between the parabolic characters of $\pm\Gamma$ and those of $\Gamma$, which permits period computations to be carried out on the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$. It is used in the comparison of cup pairings under conjugation ([`ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair_comp_eq_of_conjRel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair_comp_eq_of_conjRel)) and in the rank formula [`ModularCurve.six_mul_level_mul_finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_add_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.six_mul_level_mul_finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_add_eq).
